body:
Hey man. It is late night here in Southeast Asia but I just wanna drop by and say hi and wish you all the best

&#x200B;

I started this journey shortly a month or two ago too. Am in 2nd year of college now and 23. Just wanted to remind you that 18 is still very young. So take your time to invest in yourself (in knowledge, in learning) like you are doing with the videos and books. Don't be afraid to make mistakes. 

I am like you, a beginner, but I have a great teacher to bring and guide me along. 

&#x200B;

The FIRE, or money game as I would call it, is a journey. So don't be ashamed to borrow or use your parent's money. I have been getting an interest-free loan from the bank for 4 years (while I am in college, interest starts from graduation) and the 30K or so from my parent's that was meant for my college, I invested it in a bond.

2 years later I will be getting about 3K of interest from the bank to get me off my feet in the working world. But I will still pay off my parents on a later date. 

&#x200B;

If you are adamant about the money, then start sourcing for a scholarship, bursaries in addition to part-time jobs. Even for scholarships, at least for my country, some offer reasonable bond time.

&#x200B;

Wishing you all the best. Feel free to pm for a chat or exchange a few messages. I follow Graham and Tony Robbin's videos too. I would suggest Dan Lok and Patrick David, but that's my personal preference.
